# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# This site uses real URLs (/faq, /agenda, /complete-profile) resolved by
# React Router in the browser. Without this rule the host looks for a file at
# that path, doesn't find one, and returns 404 — which breaks page refreshes
# and, more importantly, the "Complete my profile" link in every confirmation
# email, since that link opens a deep URL directly from the inbox.
#
# Vite copies everything in public/ to dist/, so this ends up at dist/_redirects
# where Netlify picks it up.
#
# Not on Netlify? Delete this file and use the equivalent for your host:
#   Vercel       - vercel.json in the repo root (included)
#   Nginx        - try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
#   Apache       - .htaccess with FallbackResource /index.html
#   GitHub Pages - copy dist/index.html to dist/404.html after building
#   Cloudflare   - a _redirects file works there too, same syntax

/*    /index.html   200
